<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Reward Aggregation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Actor preference dataset with length control.</span>
Given the prompt:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle\mathrm{on-chainmetrics}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>on</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>chainmetrics</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle\mathrm{on-chainmetrics},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{newsdigest},\mathrm{sentimentsnapshot}\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>newsdigest</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>sentimentsnapshot</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{newsdigest},\mathrm{sentimentsnapshot}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">the actor model generates <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> candidates <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y_{t}^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{t}^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> using nucleus sampling (<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>). Each candidate is evaluated <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> times, with malformed outputs discarded and scores averaged to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{S}_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{S}_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> as the highest/lowest scores. A tunable threshold <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> partitions scores:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Top-tier}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>tier</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Top-tier}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[(1-\rho)S_{\max}+\rho S_{\min},S_{\max}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[(1-\rho)S_{\max}+\rho S_{\min},S_{\max}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Low-tier}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Low</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>tier</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Low-tier}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[S_{\min},(1-\rho)S_{\min}+\rho S_{\max}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[S_{\min},(1-\rho)S_{\min}+\rho S_{\max}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Select the shortest top-tier candidate as positive <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and longest low-tier as negative <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Judge preference dataset via Elo aggregation.</span>
Adapt Elo rating with: Dynamic <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{t}=K_{\mathrm{base}}\cdot(1+\sigma_{t}/\sigma_{\max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{t}=K_{\mathrm{base}}\cdot(1+\sigma_{t}/\sigma_{\max})</annotation></semantics></math> and Non-zero-sum adjustment as</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E3X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{Elo}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Elo</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathrm{Elo}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=K\cdot\Big(I[r_{\mathrm{model}}&gt;r_{\mathrm{market}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>market</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=K\cdot\Big(I[r_{\mathrm{model}}&gt;r_{\mathrm{market}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E3Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{1+10^{(S_{\mathrm{opponent}}-S_{\mathrm{model}})/400}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>opponent</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{1+10^{(S_{\mathrm{opponent}}-S_{\mathrm{model}})/400}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For high-variance forecasts, form judgment pairs <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j^{(m)},j^{(n)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j^{(m)},j^{(n)})</annotation></semantics></math> and record wins in matrix <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{mn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{mn}</annotation></semantics></math> with order-normalized weights <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{1},\omega_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{1},\omega_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Compute Elo scores by maximizing:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m,n}B_{mn}\log\sigma(\varepsilon_{m}-\varepsilon_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m,n}B_{mn}\log\sigma(\varepsilon_{m}-\varepsilon_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Select highest- and lowest-scoring judgments as positive/negative samples, discarding verbose pairs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Generalized Preference-based Reinforcement Optimization</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We incorporate a reinforcement learning strategy inspired by Generalized Preference-based Reinforcement Optimization (GPRO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al. (2024)</a></cite> to optimize the actor, judge, and meta-judge in a closed feedback loop. At each training step, the actor samples two candidate responses, which are evaluated based on precomputed criteria. These evaluations result in reward vectors <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{r}_{t}^{(1)},\mathbf{r}_{t}^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{r}_{t}^{(1)},\mathbf{r}_{t}^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math>, which are passed through an aggregation MLP to produce scalar rewards <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}_{t}^{(i)}=f_{\mathrm{agg}}(\mathbf{r}_{t}^{(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>agg</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}_{t}^{(i)}=f_{\mathrm{agg}}(\mathbf{r}_{t}^{(i)})</annotation></semantics></math>. These scalar rewards form input pairs <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math> for the meta-judge, which models the preference between them. The meta-judge is trained with a DPO-style loss:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{meta}}=-\log p," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>meta</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{meta}}=-\log p,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\sigma\left(M_{\phi}(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\sigma\left(M_{\phi}(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the sigmoid function. The preference probability <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> should approach 1 when <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is truly better, guiding the meta-judge to favor higher-quality outputs. The meta-judge’s parameters <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> are updated accordingly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To efficiently propagate the preference signal, a lightweight judge <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is trained to approximate the meta-judge’s behavior. The judge is trained using a supervised regression objective to minimize the discrepancy between the meta-judge and judge’s preferences:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{align}}=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(M_{\phi}(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})-M_{\theta}(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})\right)^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>align</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{align}}=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(M_{\phi}(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})-M_{\theta}(r_{t}^{(1)},r_{t}^{(2)})\right)^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This allows the judge to distill the preference knowledge from the meta-judge, enabling efficient evaluation during actor fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For actor optimization, preference pairs <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j_{c},j_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j_{c},j_{r})</annotation></semantics></math> are constructed from the actor’s outputs, where <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is the candidate with the higher Elo aggregation score, and <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> has the lower score. These pairs are used to optimize the actor’s policy, encouraging it to produce outputs similar to <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> while suppressing those resembling <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. The training objective is:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{actor}}=\mathbb{E}\left[\log\frac{\exp(\pi_{\theta}(j_{c})/\beta)}{\exp(\pi_{\theta}(j_{c})/\beta)+\exp(\pi_{\theta}(j_{r})/\beta)}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>actor</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{actor}}=\mathbb{E}\left[\log\frac{\exp(\pi_{\theta}(j_{c})/\beta)}{\exp(\pi_{\theta}(j_{c})/\beta)+\exp(\pi_{\theta}(j_{r})/\beta)}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the actor policy and <math id="S3.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a temperature parameter.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Our approach mitigates overfitting through two mechanisms: (1) the self-supervised preference signals are comparative and robust to noise, and (2) joint training of generation and evaluation modules regularizes each other. As shown in our experiments, the model exhibits strong generalization despite frequent market regime shifts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>
<span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparative Performance Against State-of-the-art Baselines.</span>
Our Meta-RL approach demonstrates superior risk-adjusted returns compared to state-of-the-art language models (GPT-4, Gemini) and specialized financial AI systems (DeepSeek, DMind), with particularly strong performance in challenging bear market conditions (-8% vs. -12% to -22%).
</figcaption>
<div id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:56.7pt;vertical-align:-26.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-89.3pt,14.7pt) scale(0.658794131495891,0.658794131495891) ;">
<table id="S3.T2.4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T2.4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total Return (%)</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Daily Return (%)</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="3"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sharpe Ratio</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bull</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sideways</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bear</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bull</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sideways</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bear</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bull</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sideways</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bear</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
